From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lane-a <lane@example.invalid>
Date: Mon, 2 Mar 2026 10:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] stock: reorder at the threshold

reorder_needed() compared with < so a level exactly at the threshold never
triggered a reorder. tests/test_stock.py passes.
---
 CHANGELOG.md | 1 +
 inv/stock.py | 2 +-
 2 files changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/CHANGELOG.md b/CHANGELOG.md
index d8288e4..d9cc06b 100644
--- a/CHANGELOG.md
+++ b/CHANGELOG.md
@@ -3,4 +3,5 @@
 
 ## Unreleased
 
+- Reorder is now needed at the reorder level, not only below it.
 - Initial stock, units and report modules.
diff --git a/inv/stock.py b/inv/stock.py
index 9f20adb..df44676 100644
--- a/inv/stock.py
+++ b/inv/stock.py
@@ -12,7 +12,7 @@ class Stock:
 
     def reorder_needed(self):
         """True when stock is at or below the reorder level."""
-        return self.on_hand < self.reorder_level
+        return self.on_hand <= self.reorder_level
 
     def reserve(self, qty):
         """Take QTY out of stock; the level is kept to 2 decimals."""
